meta {
  name: List subject offerings
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subject-offerings?section_id={{sectionId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.count: eq 2
  res.body.page.limit: eq 50
  res.body.page.offset: eq 0
  res.body.page.has_more: eq false
}

docs {
  Maths and French, the two offerings 05/02 and 05/03 made for this section.
  Filtering by section_id is what keeps that count honest whatever else the
  tenant holds.

  Note what is not passed: academic_session_id. Without it the query is
  already restricted to the current session, so a listing never quietly
  spreads across years. all_sessions=true is the explicit way to ask for the
  whole history.

  Like sections, offerings have no breadth key: SubjectOfferingsRead is
  read/write/delete only. An offering describes a timetable slot, not a
  person, so there is nothing to narrow per caller.
}
